Revision history for Authen-WebAuthn
 
Unreleased
  - Fix PS256 signature verification (32 byte salt)
  - Fix trust_anchors given as a code reference
  - A trust anchor that is not a PEM certificate is refused as such. It
    made every attestation fail, or with allow_untrusted_attestation,
    made every attestation Self without an error.
  - Decode client-supplied CBOR with a decoder for the subset WebAuthn
    uses: tags (which could instantiate Perl objects or expand to
    gigabytes), floats, undefined, indefinite lengths, integers of 2^53
    or more, duplicate map keys and map keys that are neither integers
    nor text strings are refused, as is data holding more than 10,000
    items or nested more than 16 deep, which bounds the memory a response
    can take
  - The stored credential public key given to validate_assertion is read
    by the same decoder, so it must be CBOR as an authenticator writes it,
    which the credential_pubkey returned by validate_registration is. A
    key encoded from a Perl hash with CBOR::XS, whose map labels are
    strings, is refused.
  - At registration, reject a credential public key that does not parse,
    whose key type does not match its algorithm, or an RSA key outside
    2048 to 4096 bits or with an exponent over 32 bytes. A stored RSA key
    is read up to 8192 bits, with an exponent up to 128 bytes, at sign-in.
  - COSE key type, algorithm and curve must be CBOR integers
  - ES256 is refused with a key that is not on P-256: packed attestation
    accepted an ES256 statement signed by a P-384 certificate key
  - Malformed input is refused with a message of its own, without Perl
    errors or warnings
  - Reject credential IDs longer than 1023 bytes
  - Authenticator data whose extension data flag is set must hold
    extension data, and it must be a CBOR map: a flag with nothing after
    it, or an array, was accepted before
  - Refuse an attestation format that is not a text string, and an
    attestation statement that is not a map, with the none format too
  - An attestation certificate without Basic Constraints is refused as
    such, not with a Perl error
  - Looking up an unknown algorithm no longer adds it to the table of
    supported algorithms
  - Authen::WebAuthn::Test produces RSA keys, packed self attestation,
    and packed and fido-u2f attestation with a certificate

0.005
  - Add allow_unknown_attestation_format option

0.004
  - Add allow_untrusted_attestation option

0.003 2023-11-09
  - Update Crypt::OpenSSL::X509::Extension and Net::SSLeay dependancies
  - Make sure Net::SSLeay is initialized before use

0.002 2023-11-09
  - Supported attestation types: none, packed, fido-u2f
  - Mandatory attestation trust chain validation

0.001 2022-01-21
  - initial release
  - Authentication and registration without attestation
  - ECC/RSA keys supported
